  "description": "Save an Excel workbook (DocWright.Spreadsheet) as PDF, images or HTML, with each sheet on the pages Excel prints it on; managed .NET, no Office, no interop, no need for the DocWright Word package. SpreadsheetConverter writes PDF as Excel's own export does (tagged PDF and PDF/A on request), page images, a range or a chart as a picture, and one self-contained HTML page; cell text, number formats, fills, borders, conditional formats, pictures, charts, shapes and sparklines are drawn, following the sheet's page setup. SpreadsheetLayout gives the same page model DocWright's PDF and image renderers draw, and SpreadsheetGeometry gives a grid view the column and row positions of a sheet on screen.",
